327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (This insight shows which states have the highest in-state tuition burden when tuition is compared to median household income rather than just listed by raw tuition alone. That makes the analysis more meaningful because a state with moderate tuition can still be less affordable if income is lower. The main conclusion is that affordability changes when economic context is added, and that raw tuition by itself does not tell the full story. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
