358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (This clustering analysis groups states into three distinct categories based on tuition, student debt, household income, and educational attainment. The results show a clear pattern: one cluster represents high-income, highly educated states with significantly higher tuition levels, while another cluster represents lower-income, less educated states with lower tuition. A third cluster falls in between, showing moderate values across all variables. This suggests that college costs are not randomly distributed but instead closely tied to broader socioeconomic conditions within each state.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
